--TEST--
a request answers the scheme it was decided to have, and null where it had no peer to name `rule:http-server/trusted-proxies-is-empty-and-empty-reads-nothing` `rule:errors/ambiguous-input-refused`
--SCHEME--
https
--GET--
page=2
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A request that named a scheme and no other peer fact. `https` is a claim only
// the door can make — a connection that was not itself TLS reads it from a
// trusted proxy or not at all — so the answer is never derived from anything
// this program can see.
echo Core\Request::scheme(), "\n";
// `null` is an answer and not a hole waiting to be filled: a peer with no
// address to report and a request that named no authority are both facts, and
// `""` or `"0.0.0.0"` for either is the repair
// `rule:errors/ambiguous-input-refused` forbids.
echo Core\Request::clientIp() ?? "none", "\n";
echo Core\Request::host() ?? "none", "\n";
// The request is still a request: the query it carried reads back as usual, so
// the two nulls above are answers about the peer rather than a program running
// with nothing inbound.
echo Core\Request::query("page") ?? "", "\n";
--EXPECT--
https
none
none
2
